# TraaS + Tech Bootcamp Project Rules

## Product scope
- Build a cases website for two tracks: TraaS and Tech Bootcamp.
- Include: landing page, two case-list pages, single case page, user account, AI assistant placeholder.

## Required stack
- Next.js (App Router), Tailwind CSS, Supabase (DB/Auth/Storage), Vercel.

## Work process (mandatory)
- Do not implement "everything at once"; ship in small verified stages.
- Start each stage with: analysis, architecture, and file-level change plan.
- Build order: scaffold -> UI pages -> case data model -> filters -> case detail -> Supabase -> auth/account -> case form -> roles -> AI placeholder -> QA -> deploy prep.
- Keep temporary mock data until real integration is confirmed working.

## Design and UX
- Use reference style direction from `techbootcamp-alumni.netlify.app` without 1:1 copying.
- Keep UI modern, clean, mobile-first, and product-oriented.
- Clearly differentiate TraaS and Tech Bootcamp in visuals and content labels.

## Data model baseline
- Case entity must support: track type, title, slug, company, author, role, short and full descriptions, challenge, solution, result, tags, year/date, cover image, publish status.

## Agent guardrails
- Explain plan first, then implement.
- Show which files will be created/changed before edits.
- Do not delete existing files or major sections without user confirmation.
- Do not commit or deploy unless explicitly requested.